==English==
[[File:Velociraptor_Restoration.png|thumb]]

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|NL.|-}} {{taxfmt|Velociraptor|genus}} genus name, from {{af|la|vēlōx|gloss1=swift|raptor|gloss2=thief|nocat=1}}.

The application to {{taxfmt|Deinonychus|genus}} came about because Gregory S. Paul proposed that {{taxfmt|Velociraptor|genus}} and {{taxfmt|Deinonychus|genus}} were the same genus<ref>{{cite-book
|author=Gregory S. Paul
|authorlink=Gregory S. Paul
|title=Predatory Dinosaurs of the World
|location=New York, London, Toronto, Sydney, Tokyo
|publisher=Simon and Schuster
|year=1988
|page=364|isbn=0-671-61946-2
}}</ref> and this idea was taken up in the book leading to the [[w:Jurassic Park|''Jurassic Park'']] film series.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/vəˌlɒsɪˈɹæptɚ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[agile]] [[dinosaur]], of the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Velociraptor|genus}}, having [[sickle]]-[[shaped]] [[claw]]s. It is also thought to have had a feathered coat. Fossils have been found in Late Cretaceous deposits [[Mongolia]] and [[China]] (around 75-71 mya).
